   "etymology": "Likely from Proto-Albanian *wadza, from Proto-Indo-European *woǵʰ-eh₂, from *weǵʰ- (“to bring, carry”), cognate with Proto-Germanic *wegaz (“way, path”). Alternatively:\n* from Proto-Albanian *wada with unexpected aspiration, from Proto-Indo-European *wodʰ-eh₂, from *wedʰ- (“to lead; to bring”) or *wedʰ- (“to beat, strike”);\n* or borrowed from Ancient Greek ὁδός (hodós, “way, road”).\nBy some identified as the source of Ancient Greek οὔθα (oútha, “dust; way, road”).",
